WEBVTT

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.230
And on stage A, the third of the 
second round matches has just begun.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:14.510
Of the top sixteen schools, 
only two schools remain

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.150
for which this is their first 
appearance at the inter-high.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.240
The strong win and the weak are defeated.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.100
That is the rule of the inter-high.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.250
It is a veritable survival of the fittest.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.550
One of those schools is 
Nagano's Kiyosumi High School.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.760
It's a young team, with three 
first years playing as regulars.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.400
Yuuki, their first player,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.250
is one of the first year trio.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.060
With Kataoka as the opening dealer, 
the game begins!

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.060
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:17.670
<b>Hand 4: 
East Wind</b>

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:24.290
<i>She's...</i>

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.790
The one to watch out for in the first 
players' match is Kiyosumi's Kataoka.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.290
Kiyosumi?

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.170
Not Eisui?

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.190
Yes.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.800
This dumb-looking girl?

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.720
Of course, Eisui is strong, so 
we can't let our guard down.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.550
But before that, we have 
to deal with Kataoka.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:46.310
This creature's record in the 
regional tournament was frightening.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.890
She holds the all-time high score 
in the individual tournament,

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.160
but only for the East round of the first day.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.880
That's ridiculous.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.540
Since I was curious, I got some 
statistics I usually don't look at,

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.300
and realized that the odds of her being

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.570
the opening dealer are high, for some reason.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:05.600
Isn't there just a one-in-four chance 
of getting any seat in the dice roll?

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.200
That's usually how it goes.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.390
That means we might have

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.390
to consider her a being that isn't 
bound by common sense...

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.480
<i>I never thought she'd really be the first dealer.</i>

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.050
<i>What will she do?</i>

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.140
Riichi!

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.900
<i>A dealer's riichi! On the third turn!</i>

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.530
Kiyosumi's Kataoka has already 
managed a riichi as dealer

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.280
on the third turn of East Hand 1!

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.150
This was pretty quick.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:46.910
Kataoka did not draw a single 
useless tile before her riichi.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:51.410
How will the other three players 
go up against this riichi?

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:55.210
<i>I guess Eisui's Jindai is out of this hand.</i>

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.860
<i>2 of circles.</i>

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.810
I'm tired...

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.680
How about this?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.480
<i>Straight into unknown territory!</i>

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:13.440
Pon.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:14.390
Huh?

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.810
<i>Weren't you out of the game?</i>

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.070
<i>I don't get it...</i>

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.310
<i>If it wasn't for that pon, this 
would have been Kiyosumi's...</i>

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:28.950
<i>Could this be her winning tile?!</i>

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:48.470
Tsumo!

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.840
That's 4,000 all!

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.120
<i>If not for that pon, she would've gotten</i>

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.360
<i>a sanshoku and ippatsu for a dealer's baiman.</i>

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.630
<i>That would've been 8,000 all.</i>

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.140
Suzu-chan's job is to keep

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:08.870
the gap between us and the 
top place to within 30,000 points.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.240
<i>That's not going to be 
easy with this crowd.</i>

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:16.370
You better do it, or it's permanent 
marker on your forehead!

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:18.930
<b>Shame</b>

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.830
<i>She won even though 
we changed the order.</i>

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.760
<i>This is nothing like what I heard.</i>

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.760
<i>That feeling in my fingertips...</i>

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.650
<i>Didn't Noppo train me so that</i>

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.020
<i>having the order changed wouldn't affect me?</i>

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.810
<i>They're all... alive!</i>

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.580
What's wrong?

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:43.230
You seem worn out all of a sudden.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:44.470
Huh?

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:45.960
Ever since we entered the South round,

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.070
I can't feel your power at all.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.620
It's like when a cloud moves in front of the moon.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.430
It's like, whenever we get into the South round,

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.210
I can't seem to concentrate.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:00.380
I wish it was just an East match...

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.370
Hmm.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.710
Then why don't you go on 
a streak in the East round

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:06.540
and end the match there?

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:11.140
If you do that, then it's always an East match!

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.890
She's got a point.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.650
All right. I'm just going to 
end it here by going on a streak!

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:20.780
Wha—

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:25.280
This game isn't going to have an East Hand 2!

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:28.620
<i>What did she just say?</i>

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.620
<i>She's going to end it in East Hand 1?</i>

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:35.410
<i>Even if we'd each started with 25,000 
points, you'd be considered crazy.</i>

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.730
<i>But here, we've got 100,000 points!</i>

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.870
<i>If she actually manages to take</i>

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:43.170
<i>those 100,000 points while she's the dealer,</i>

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.240
<i>she'd be one of the most</i>

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:47.660
<i>fearsome monsters the 
inter-high has ever seen.</i>

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:49.340
The dice?

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.640
Oh, yeah!

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:56.470
<i>Was that just some trash talk?</i>

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.940
<i>She doesn't really look 
like someone who could</i>

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.730
<i>take 100,000 points from us.</i>

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.780
<i>Maybe she's just an airhead...</i>

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:06.140
<i>She's going to be bothersome.</i>

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:11.430
On Stage A, we're in the first half 
of the third first players' match.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:14.410
Kataoka has opened the match 
with a dealer mangan tsumo win.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:18.840
Pro player Kainou, what do you make 
of the hand we just witnessed?

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:22.100
Looking at Kataoka's records so far,

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:25.170
it seems that her concentration is
quite extraordinary in the early game.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:29.050
This last win she had was 
probably par for the course.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:34.110
Indeed, Kataoka's East round 
performance is extremely good.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.610
In any case, what's most important in

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:39.800
the first players' match is to 
bank points while you can.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:44.020
The other three players also hit quite hard.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.660
The one to watch for among them

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:50.400
is Eisui Girls' Jindai Komaki.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:51.800
Yes.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.490
I am personally watching her closely.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:57.720
Very closely.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.660
East Hand 1

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.660
Bonus 1

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.080
Aw, man, no tenhou!

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:05.770
<i>A tanyao hand with two dora guaranteed.</i>

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:08.050
<i>It looks like I can call and 
end her turn as dealer quickly.</i>

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:10.340
Chi!

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.410
<i>One tile from tenpai!</i>

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:15.800
Come on!

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:20.390
Pon!

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:23.280
<i>Right on.</i>

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:24.460
<i>I'm in tenpai.</i>

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:29.820
Ron!

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:35.280
I didn't have to wait for a new hand after all.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.240
8,000!

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:40.790
<i>I was told that in the East round,</i>

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.670
<i>Kataoka declares riichi as soon as she can.</i>

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:47.530
<i>Suehara-senpai, this isn't 
the way you said it'd be!</i>

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.750
<i>Just calm down.</i>

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.670
<i>The game has just begun.</i>

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:56.640
<i>I was a regular at a strong 
school in my first year, too!</i>

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.890
<i>This is just the start.</i>

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.100
East Hand 1

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:00.100
Bonus 2

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.140
Double riichi!

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.310
<i>She's unfazed?</i>

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:10.700
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:14.900
<i>Fast riichis...</i>

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.630
<i>I've heard some superstition about them.</i>

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.730
<i>There's no way to know for sure.</i>

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:21.290
<i>I'll just play my regular.</i>

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:25.080
<i>If that's her tile, it'll just be like an accident.</i>

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:27.880
Ron! Ippatsu!

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:32.000
<i>Is that seriously her winning tile?!</i>

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:36.520
7,700 plus the two bonuses... That's 8,300!

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:39.600
This is Kataoka's third consecutive win 
since the beginning of the East round.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.330
And that's twice in a row

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.970
Himematsu's Ueshige dealt into Kiyosumi's hand.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.050
Yuuki-chan's amazing!

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:48.910
That's her third consecutive win!

00:09:48.910 --> 00:09:52.730
Well, I guess she's not doing too badly.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.900
Is it so hard to just admit 
that she's doing good?

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.930
With her, it's always from 
this point that things change.

00:09:58.930 --> 00:09:59.920
That's right.

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:04.040
And her opponents know that Yuuki's 
only strong in the East round.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:05.620
Even so...

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.660
<b>Himematsu</b>

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.970
This is getting off to a pretty bad start!

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:13.680
Ueshige-san... are you going to be okay?

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:14.950
No worries.

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:16.920
Everything thus far was accounted for.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:20.620
<i>Just do your job, Suzu-chan.</i>

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.560
<i>Damn...</i>

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:31.440
<i>Now she's got a 48,600 point lead.</i>

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.610
East Hand 1

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.610
Bonus 3

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:39.470
<i>I guess even she doesn't get 
consecutive double riichis.</i>

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:50.270
<i>My hand stopped at a point where 
I would normally never hesitate...</i>

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:52.410
<i>Discarding the 5 of characters would leave</i>

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.970
<i>the most possible ways to get into tenpai.</i>

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:00.720
<i>But I'm concerned about 
the player across from me,</i>

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:03.180
<i>Eisui's Jindai.</i>

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.720
<i>She's so quiet, there's 
something not right about it.</i>

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:09.600
Li'l time out.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:10.850
<i>Here she goes.</i>

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:12.410
<i>"Li'l time out."</i>

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:15.190
Next, we have Miyamori's Kosegawa.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:18.290
Watch out for when she's 
not sure what to discard.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.860
That's typically when she's building
a really expensive hand.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.010
What's weird is that it doesn't look like

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:27.230
she's hesitating on how to make 
her hand more expensive,

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:30.200
but like her hand gets expensive 
because she hesitated.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:34.130
<i>If she hesitates, her hand gets expensive.</i>

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:35.950
<i>Kosegawa Shiromi.</i>

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:37.810
I've made up my mind.

00:11:37.810 --> 00:11:39.130
This is kinda weird, but here goes.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:50.560
I'm sorry. I fell asleep for a bit.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.720
What?!

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.690
You've been playing with your 
eyes open this whole time!

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:55.720
My score has gone down...

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:59.010
I'm sorry, this happens 
sometimes when I'm tired.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:01.700
I'm really sorry, but from here out,

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:04.200
I'll be playing with more than my full strength.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:09.060
<i>Suddenly...</i>

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:11.200
<i>This is looking bad!</i>

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:13.660
Ah.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.920
Hey, which game should we go watch?

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.350
<b>Kiyosumi</b>

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:38.060
Huh?

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.120
What's wrong?

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.890
Nothing...

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:48.330
<i>I just had a feeling like a new power was...</i>

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.640
<i>not appearing, but more like disappearing...</i>

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.850
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka) 
2nd Year 
Ueshige Suzu

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.080
<i>She was asleep?</i>

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.120
<i>Is she joking?</i>

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.600
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate) 
3rd Year 
Kosegawa Shiromi

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.500
<i>I don't want things to get bothersome.</i>

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.980
Kiyosumi High School 
(Nagano)
1st Year
Kataoka Yuuki

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:02.130
<i>For a moment, she felt 
like Saki-chan does.</i>

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.610
Eisui Girls' School 
(Kagoshima)
2nd Year
Jindai Komaki

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:08.180
<i>This shrine priestess scares me a little.</i>

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:11.520
<i>But I've got a triplet of dora, 
and I'm one tile from tenpai.</i>

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:14.140
<i>I can still put the pressure on.</i>

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:22.900
<i>A dora...</i>

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.980
<i>I'm in tenpai for a dealer 
mangan in the third turn.</i>

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:31.120
<i>This hand is mine, too!</i>

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:41.580
<i>Tenpai...</i>

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.880
<i>Bamboo, eh?</i>

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.900
<i>I managed to get a head start 
against these players...</i>

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.620
<i>This could work.</i>

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:02.150
Riichi!

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:07.620
Huh?

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.610
<i>She's discarding one of those already?</i>

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.080
<i>She's discarding her draw, too?</i>

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:19.990
<i>Wait... could these two be in tenpai, too?</i>

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:24.210
<i>But then I might deal into 
one of their hands again...</i>

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.520
Oh, that! Ron!

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.080
Menpin, ippatsu.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.080
[Menpin: menzen (closed hand) + pinfu]

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:38.730
With two ura dora and 
three bonuses, that's 8,900.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:40.520
Y-Yes!

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:42.070
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:45.740
<i>I thought Eisui's player was gonna get serious.</i>

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:54.550
Wow, it looks like the princess 
is completely awake now.

00:14:54.550 --> 00:14:56.700
She woke up early this time.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.670
Once Komaki-chan is awake, 
she works really hard.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.570
I feel like this is the first time

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:06.400
she's woken up this early in 
a match that wasn't against us.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:08.130
Doesn't look like she's going 
to fall back asleep, either.

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:12.050
I think we should be prepared 
for about a 30,000 point gap.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:16.720
Even if it's a 60,000 point gap, I'll handle it.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.370
If the gap gets to 90,000,

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:20.640
shall we cut out all snacks for today?

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:23.650
As long as she doesn't go bust, who cares?

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:26.540
That's true.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.900
Let's just sit back and see how it goes.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:32.950
Jun, hurry up!

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:35.410
Yuuki's match is going to be over!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.080
You're the one who asked me 
to go to the restroom with you.

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.720
Yeah, because going alone is sca—

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:41.080
I mean...

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:43.250
Never mind.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.270
I guess it's more than your 
short stature that makes you a kid.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.230
<i>She's huge!</i>

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:03.750
Compared to that person, 
you're a kid, too!

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:07.840
Now, hold on. Seeing a woman 
taller than me is quite rare.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:10.950
But then, I've never seen a 
teen smaller than you, either.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.280
Who is that?

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:17.460
<b>Miyamori Girls'</b>

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:19.480
I'm back!

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:21.080
Welcome back, Toyone.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.710
How's Jindai-san doing?

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:27.420
Don't ask about the enemy.
Ask about Shiro, who's on your team.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:31.270
But... Jindai-san is really great.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.190
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
3rd Year
Anetai Toyone

00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:33.510
Last year, she totally 
dominated Fujiwara Risa

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.740
from Kyuushuu's Sekizan High School.

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:38.930
Then why don't you 
get her autograph?

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:38.910
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
3rd Year
Kakura Kurumi

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.200
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
3rd Year
Aislinn Wishart

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.750
Yes, I'll do that...

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:43.710
Miyamori Girls' (Iwate)
3rd Year
Ususawa Sae

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:46.690
After we've defeated Eisui 
and taken first place.

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.940
On Stage A, the third of 
the second round matches.

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:53.600
After three consecutive wins by 
Kiyosumi's Kataoka, the first dealer,

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:55.400
Eisui Girls' Jindai dealt into a

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.590
mangan hand from Himematsu 
High School's Ueshige.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:03.460
This ends the long East Hand 1. 
We're now moving into East Hand 2.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:06.690
Now for the current point totals.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.710
Kiyosumi High School's Kataoka is

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.460
currently in the lead with 128,300 points.

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:15.470
Following her is Miyamori Girls' 
Kosegawa with 96,000 points.

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:19.900
Himematsu High School's 
Ueshige has 88,600 points.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:24.480
And Eisui Girls' Jindai has 87,100 points.

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.440
And now, East Hand 2 begins.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:34.350
<i>My turn as dealer... my precious 
turn as dealer is gone!</i>

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:39.570
<i>But we're still in the East round, 
and that's all that matters!</i>

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:41.450
<i>I can still fight!</i>

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:55.300
<i>All right!</i>

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.680
<i>My starting hand is already one tile from tenpai!</i>

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.060
<i>No way...</i>

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:11.790
<i>It happened!</i>

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.800
<i>If I discard the same wind to get to
 tenpai, the hand will be a draw.</i>

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:16.420
<i>And I had such a good hand...</i>

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:18.660
<i>If I break it up, I'll kill my momentum...</i>

00:18:19.190 --> 00:18:21.370
<i>As if. That's just stupid.</i>

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:25.830
<i>If my momentum would 
disappear just from that,</i>

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.620
<i>I don't even want it!</i>

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:32.500
To avoid a draw, Kiyosumi's 
Kataoka breaks up her tenpai.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.510
Turn 8

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.630
<i>And I'm back in tenpai!</i>

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:41.080
Riichi!

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.930
<i>I'm not going to stay quiet here!</i>

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.860
<i>There's something odd about this riichi.</i>

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:06.420
She should've just stayed quiet.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:08.100
Now that she's declared riichi,

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.390
everyone could have dropped out.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:12.080
I wonder about that.

00:19:12.390 --> 00:19:13.410
<i>For one second,</i>

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.590
<i>it looked like Kosegawa was 
hesitating about which tile to discard.</i>

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:19.800
<i>Be careful, Suzu-chan.</i>

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:25.210
Ippatsu, it is not.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:45.160
Mayoiga...?

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.120
It feels like something's about to happen.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.170
Yes.

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:54.490
The more Kosegawa Shiromi hesitates,

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:56.520
the more expensive her hand gets.

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:57.670
Almost like...

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:01.170
...the ancient folk tale from the Touno region.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:05.490
The legendary house that bestows 
riches upon all who visit it...

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:07.960
Mayoiga, "house of the lost."

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:15.620
<i>Finally.</i>

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.920
<i>She discarded a strong one...</i>

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:27.300
<i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:34.290
A traveler on a mountain path

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:37.560
wanders along, lost, until...

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:46.430
Within a black gate...

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:54.710
He finds a mansion with a courtyard 
overrun with white and red flowers.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.220
This one was pretty deep.

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:04.900
Tsumo.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:06.780
3,000. 6,000.

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:12.540
In East Hand 2, Miyamori's 
Kosegawa gets a haneman tsumo!

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:15.010
She turned her score positive again in one go!

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:18.710
Finally, a Shiro-like win!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.930
Looks like the second round 
match should go okay, too.

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:21.800
Yeah!

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:26.450
Man, she got her chance 
snatched from her twice now.

00:21:26.450 --> 00:21:27.550
Yuuki...

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.550
Is Suzu going to be okay?!

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:35.940
This is still within our expectations.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.560
The problem starts from here on out...

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:40.440
Hit 'em hard, Suzu-chan!

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:43.860
Just when I thought the momentum 
Kiyosumi had was gone,

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.670
now it's with Miyamori?

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:49.600
There's no telling how big the gap will get.

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:51.200
Yeah...

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:54.200
<i>When we came down from the mountain,</i>

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:57.960
<i>it may have just been a coincidence 
that they were coming down</i>

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.010
<i>from a mountain at the same time.</i>

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:03.130
<i>What do you think, Komaki-chan?</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Gods and Demons</b>

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:38.090
Hey, did you know...

00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:40.490
the biggest producer of kiwi fruit

00:23:40.490 --> 00:23:42.980
isn't New Zealand, but Italy?

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:44.010
For real?!

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:46.210
New Zealand is actually the third biggest.

00:23:46.210 --> 00:23:48.230
Good to know.

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:55.100
<b>Please Watch Again</b>
